abstract: >-
  PhysDiagTwin is a lightweight physics-aware digital twin framework for controlled fault-data generation and diagnostic evaluation in a fan-driven
  thermal process. It integrates a reduced-order dynamic process model, severity-controlled fault perturbation, bidirectional MQTT communication,
  automated Node-RED experiment orchestration, traceable ground truth, and leakage-aware machine-learning evaluation. The framework supports controlled
  investigation of mechanical imbalance, electrical overcurrent, cooling degradation, and thermal overload across programmed fault severity levels.
